 "deductions": [
  "D1. The best file is a DISCOVERY field, not a catalogue re-tracer: 78% of its 172,974 pixels lie >3 px from any supplied fault and only 3.7% sit on masked pixels. The 0.1563 was earned off-catalogue.",
  "D2. Adding 9,430 unmasked pixels (10,668 in total; a strict superset) moved the score by -0.0003: post-hoc unions of existing fields are at break-even. More pixels from the SAME detectors do not raise the score; a better detector does.",
  "D3. Spaced nodes vs dense ridge, same model and budget: 0.1193 vs 0.1152 (+0.0041). GEMSDOE3's local proxy (its README, audit fold) predicted +0.0924 for the same contrast. The local proxies over-reward sparsity by ~23\u00d7; the emission geometry is a second-order effect on the real board.",
  "D4. Training on catalogue-gap (SGMC) pixels only scored 0.0830 vs 0.1193 for the same architecture with the union target: the SGMC gap population does NOT resemble the expert new-fault set. Any strategy that leans on it as truth should be down-weighted.",
  "D5. CNN ensemble (0.1563) beats the pixel-wise HGB model (0.1152\u20130.1193) at similar budgets with almost disjoint supports (Jaccard 0.066): spatial context is worth ~+0.04, and the two families find different things. Their union is bounded between 'no new truth covered' and 'all TP disjoint' \u2014 the marginal rule puts the HGB pixels near break-even, so the union is a coin-flip, not a plan.",
  "D6. Every scored file emits ~3\u20133.6 % of the valid area and lands at 0.08\u20130.16; the leader is at 0.3049. At DTI 0.30 the break-even marginal hit-rate is 6.5 % (vs 3.3 % at 0.156): the leader's detector finds roughly twice the truth per emitted pixel. The gap is detection quality, not shaping.",
  "D7. The 19 supplied bands contain NO radiometric channel and only a 100 m detrended-elevation pair; the GeoDAWN release itself ships radiometric + magnetic GeoTIFF grids (22103_area1/area2_tiffs.zip) and the organizers hand out 1 m lidar links. Quaternary faults are mapped by experts from scarps in high-resolution topography; that channel is the one this family has never trained on (docs/STRATEGY.md \u00a74)."
 ],
 "irregularities": [
  "The 0.1560 row's file identity is inferred from GEMSDOE2's pre-registered upload order, not read from the submissions page \u2014 FLAGGED; confirm from the account's DrivenData history.",
  "Five accounts from one project family submitted to the same competition. The official rules (NLR/96647.pdf) and DrivenData's terms govern multiple accounts per individual; this is a compliance question for the owner, not something this repository can resolve \u2014 FLAGGED.",
  "The public/private chunking of the region is not published; the algebra therefore carries two readings of E_i (whole-footprint FP vs public-chunk FP) and the numbers are bounds, not points."
 ]
